From 8647f1976da854f121b0d929137cca666ea0234e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:05:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 112/638] [AROS] Seed PartitionAlloc from entropy.resource

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-3
AI_STATUS: implementation
ROOT_CAUSE: PartitionAlloc's private POSIX RandBytes path fell through to /dev/urandom, which AROS does not provide, and trapped while initializing PartitionAddressSpace for the first headless renderer command.
FIX_REASON: Use AROS getentropy() in bounded 256-byte chunks so PartitionAlloc obtains strong entropy through entropy.resource while honoring the AROS API limit.
SCOPE: base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc
VALIDATION: PartitionAlloc rand_util_posix.o cross-compiled for AROS; hosted run 0112 captured the prior /dev/urandom CHECK from RandBytes before this change.
RISK: Allocation initialization remains fail-closed when entropy.resource cannot satisfy a request, matching PartitionAlloc's security contract.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: first command renderer -> PartitionAddressSpace initialization -> private RandBytes /dev/urandom assumption -> native AROS entropy.resource bridge
Continues: 2d3ba2dc7a
---
 .../partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc          | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc b/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc
index 6bb4805298..b09c07c5ea 100644
--- a/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc
+++ b/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_alloc_base/rand_util_posix.cc
@@ -105,6 +105,18 @@ void RandBytes(void* output, size_t output_length) {
   if (getentropy(output, output_length) == 0) {
     return;
   }
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+  size_t offset = 0;
+  while (offset < output_length) {
+    size_t chunk = output_length - offset;
+    if (chunk > 256) {
+      chunk = 256;
+    }
+    PA_BASE_CHECK(
+        getentropy(static_cast<char*>(output) + offset, chunk) == 0);
+    offset += chunk;
+  }
+  return;
 #endif
   // If getrandom(2) above returned with an error and the /dev/urandom fallback
   // took place on Linux/ChromeOS bots, they would fail with a CHECK in
